---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Zarlino Audio"
  description="The terms that apply when you buy or use Zarlino Audio software and this website."
  canonicalURL="https://zarlinoaudio.com/legal/terms"
  schemaType="website"
>
  <main class="relative z-[1] bg-[#050505] min-h-screen pt-24 pb-24 px-6 md:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[820px] mx-auto">
      <nav class="mb-8 font-['Inter'] text-[13px] text-[#64748B]">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Zarlino Audio</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#94A3B8]">Terms of Service</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[clamp(32px,4.5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.02em]">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 font-['IBM_Plex_Mono'] text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[#64748B]">
        Version 1.0 · 2 October 2026
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 font-['Inter'] text-[16px] text-[#94A3B8] leading-[1.8] space-y-8">
        <p>
          These terms apply when you use zarlinoaudio.com or buy our software. By purchasing or using
          our software you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use the software.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">1. Our software</h2>
          <p>
            We currently sell Windows VST3 plugins (with standalone builds where provided). Current
            releases are marked as public beta: they are fully usable but may change, and you should
            keep backups of your sessions as usual. The software's licence terms — what you may and may
            not do with it — are set out in the
            <a href="/legal/license" class="text-[#00D4FF] hover:underline">License Agreement</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">2. Trial</h2>
          <p>
            Our plugins run fully functional for 14 days without a licence so you can evaluate them in
            your own sessions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">3. Prices, payment, delivery</h2>
          <p>
            Prices are shown on the product pages (US dollars; local-currency equivalents may be shown
            or charged depending on your payment method). Payments are processed by Paystack. Your
            licence key is displayed on the checkout page immediately after a successful payment —
            save it somewhere safe; if you lose it we will re-issue it to the purchase email on request.
            Any taxes payable are handled as required by law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">4. Refunds</h2>
          <p>
            Every purchase is covered by a 14-day money-back policy — see the
            <a href="/legal/refunds" class="text-[#00D4FF] hover:underline">Refund Policy</a>.
            Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under applicable consumer law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">5. Updates</h2>
          <p>
            We may release updates and fixes; we are not obliged to add features. Updates are provided
            under these same terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">6. Restrictions</h2>
          <p>
            Don't resell, share, or redistribute licence keys; don't redistribute the software itself;
            don't try to extract licence functions or bypass licensing; don't use the software
            unlawfully. Full restrictions are in the Licence Agreement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">7. Ownership, warranty, liability</h2>
          <p>
            The software and its content remain our property (and that of our licensors). The software
            is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind to the extent the law allows. To the
            extent the law allows, our total liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid
            for the product concerned. We are not liable for lost profits, lost sessions, or indirect
            losses. For paid products we do not exclude liability for fraud or anything else that
            cannot lawfully be excluded.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">8. Governing law &amp; contact</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of Ghana, and disputes are subject to the courts of
            Ghana. Contact:{' '}
            <a href="mailto:support@zarlinoaudio.com" class="text-[#00D4FF] hover:underline">support@zarlinoaudio.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class="pt-4 border-t border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.06)] text-[13px] text-[#475569]">
          Plain-language version 1.0 — pending legal review. We will publish an updated version once reviewed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
